{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Piyañjaha","html":"<article id='thag1.76'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.76 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.76 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Aṭṭhamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Eight </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Piyañjahattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Piyañjaha </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Uppatantesu nipate, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Settle down when others spring up; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nipatantesu uppate; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>spring up when others settle down. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vase avasamānesu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Remain when others have departed; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ramamānesu no rame”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>don’t delight when others delight. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Piyañjaho thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
